# Coach speech (Czech): the appraisal after the game (src/coach/appraisal.cpp).
# Same keys and variants as assets/coach/speech/en/appraisal.lang (its header documents every placeholder).
#
# Always positive, never blaming. The coach says "ty"; the player's gender is unknown: no
# second-person past tense or conditional ("vyhrál jsi", "našel jsi", "mohl bys", "abys procvičil"),
# no adjective agreeing with the player ("připravený"). Instead: nouns ("výhra", "tvoje pozice"),
# impersonal forms ("podařilo se ti", "neušlo ti", "bylo to vyhrané"), the present or future tense,
# or "we" ("hráli jsme", "vrátili jsme": masculine plural, the coach being male).
# Move numbers come after the noun, cardinal (glossary): "v tahu {n}", "do tahu {crit_no}", "tah {n}".
# A move ({move}, {crit_best} ...) is spoken as its piece ("dáma dé osm"), so a verb or a case never
# hangs on it: the noun "tah" carries them ("tah {move} získal", "místo tahu {crit_move}"), or the
# line is verbless or in the present tense ("{move} v tahu {n} získává materiál").
# Accuracy: "{acc:percent}" = "85 %" (spoken "pětaosmdesát procent"), count.percent in common.lang.
# Names inserted by {text}, {theme}, {level}:
#   appraisal.phase.*   nominatives: "zahájení" (n), "střední hra" (f), "koncovka" (f); the other
#                       cases, "{text:in}" ("ve střední hře") and "{text:past}" are in common.lang.
#   appraisal.reason.*  an adverbial right after "remíza" ("Remíza dohodou.", "Remíza, a to patem.").
#   theme.*             an infinitive phrase, lower case, no full stop, "svůj" for the player's own
#                       pieces; said after a colon or after "je důležité" (never after "snaž se":
#                       "snaž se dívat se").
#   appraisal.level.*   the level names of the coach page (coach.level.N.name), said inside „…“
#                       after "úroveň": "na úroveň „Začátečník“".
# {opening:def} is the opening's name as used inside a sentence (lower-case nominative, from the
# opening texts), always after a colon; "{opening}" alone at the start of a line.

